FINDINGS
MEDIUM (3)
  MOAT-T4-003  Package runner uses an unpinned package
    Server: cc-global (claude-code, global)
    Where: args cc-global
    Risk: The server starts from a package that is not fixed. A registry package with no exact version, a git branch head, a tarball or a URL can change at any time. Each start can download and run new, possibly malicious code without any review.
    Fix: Pin an exact version, for example npx @scope/server@1.4.2, uvx some-server==0.3.1 or a docker image digest. For a git package, pin a full 40-hex commit, as in npx github:user/repo#<40-hex> or uvx --from git+https://github.com/user/repo@<40-hex> tool. Or use a registry package with an exact version. Update the pin on purpose after review.
