LOW (2)
  MOAT-T4-004  npx runs with its yes option on (-y, --yes or npm_config_yes)
    Server: cc-global (claude-code, global)
    Where: args
    Risk: npx -y, npx --yes or an npm_config_yes env entry overrides the npm_config_yes=false that mcpmoat scan sets, so the scan itself installs and runs the package, and in a terminal npx also skips its confirmation prompt.
    Fix: Pin an exact version (see MOAT-T4-003), or install a version you reviewed and run its binary, then remove -y, --yes and npm_config_yes. Removing them alone is not enough, because an MCP client starts npx with no terminal and npx then installs a missing package with no prompt. Use npx --no or npm_config_yes=false to make npx refuse to install.
  MOAT-T4-004  npx runs with its yes option on (-y, --yes or npm_config_yes)
    Server: codex-global (codex, global)
    Where: args
    Risk: npx -y, npx --yes or an npm_config_yes env entry overrides the npm_config_yes=false that mcpmoat scan sets, so the scan itself installs and runs the package, and in a terminal npx also skips its confirmation prompt.
    Fix: Pin an exact version (see MOAT-T4-003), or install a version you reviewed and run its binary, then remove -y, --yes and npm_config_yes. Removing them alone is not enough, because an MCP client starts npx with no terminal and npx then installs a missing package with no prompt. Use npx --no or npm_config_yes=false to make npx refuse to install.
